---
description: Run the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} system-design lens on a token, component, or pattern
argument-hint: [token/component/pattern or node-id]
---
Use the **ds-steward** subagent to run its `system_design_lens` on $ARGUMENTS:
token standards (DTCG, 3-tier taxonomy, naming, intent-family completeness, scales),
component/pattern frameworks (Atomic placement, orthogonal variant axes, anatomy/API,
state completeness), reference benchmarks (DESIGN.md primary → external systems where
applicable), system-level accessibility, governance, and the **§6 heuristic canon** (system + component
layer only — Rams restraint · Shneiderman consistency · Gerhardt-Powals uncertainty-reduction ·
Weinschenk accessibility/error-prevention).

Return evidence-based findings with severity (blocker / major / minor) and a fix per
finding. Do not approve for publish until zero blockers. Do not duplicate the lens logic
here — defer to the agent.
